      "translation": {
        "english_text": "(to Vingan) On the day Sornam died... I sat just like this... she sat here... (emotionally) She fed old rice to Sokkalingam, who was that age, while I mixed the old rice with sundakkai curry and ate!... That scene still stands before my eyes...",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The cross-page Tamil syntax around `என் வயசு சொக்கலிங்கத்துக்கு` is irregular; the English renders the familial recollection conservatively without changing the closed Tamil authority."
        ]
